KNOWNBUG
interface_in_interface1.sv
--bound 0
^\[main\.p0\] always \$bits\(main\.o\.i\.x\) == 16: PROVED up to bound 0$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.o\.i\.x == main\.in: PROVED up to bound 0$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
An interface cannot instantiate another interface: inner #(W * 2) i();
gives "syntax error, unexpected '#', expecting '.' before '#'", and
inner i(); gives the same error before i. 1800-2017 A.1.4 places
interface_instantiation in module_common_item, which interface items
include via interface_or_generate_item; the parser instead accepts it
only in module_or_generate_item.
